**Read:** [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the entire relevant heterogeneous-reaction and parameter-inference treatment; [Production of Large Volume Organic Chemicals, BREF LVOC](../sources/Large-Volume-Organic-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_78ET6A4D7AX8HPQTYAMZMAG16B), a full catalytic process chapter and its operating/material history; [Production of Speciality Inorganic Chemicals, BREF SIC](../sources/Speciality-Inorganic-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_04G7NFYXE76QCB3DXCRJC1FSCP), the relevant complete catalyst/material preparation and process context.

A catalyst participates in a pathway and is regenerated by the overall catalytic cycle, but the material supplied to a plant can change through activation, restructuring, adsorption, poisoning, fouling, sintering or loss. Initial activity is one part of a full performance account. Selectivity, product quality, lifetime, separation and regeneration influence useful output.

Distinguish intrinsic site behavior from measured reactor performance. Support, pore geometry, particle shape, wetting and transport can alter which sites are accessible and what concentrations/temperatures they experience. A rate normalized by total mass may conceal a changing active fraction; a high conversion can increase an unwanted consecutive reaction.

Follow a catalyst constituent from preparation and characterization through startup, normal service, changed feed, regeneration and retirement. Reuse metals/mineral knowledge for material-state questions without assuming that a familiar composition proves the required surface structure. Keep actual proprietary preparation gaps visible in the evidence account.

**Work:** compare two documented catalysts for one complete industrial transformation on accepted product over a realistic service interval. Reconstruct activity/selectivity, transport checks, deactivation and recovery/maintenance duties. Identify an observation capable of distinguishing a chemical-site explanation from a changed physical/transport state.

**Continue:** [Connect competing reaction pathways with residence history and product isolation](Parallel-consecutive-reactions-and-where-to-stop.lingua#r_499NJSB210KGRFY8AFS5PE131S).

